<article class="env-lemma" id="0BIH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BIH">Lemma <span data-tag="0BIH">9.20.3</span>.</a> Let $L/K$ be a finite extension of fields. Let $\alpha \in L$ and let $P = x^ d + a_1 x^{d - 1} + \ldots + a_ d$ be the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $ over $K$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Norm}_{L/K}(\alpha ) = (-1)^{[L : K]} a_ d^ e \quad \text{and}\quad \text{Trace}_{L/K}(\alpha ) = - e a_1  \]
</div>
  <p> where $e d = [L : K]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BIG" data-tag="0BIG">9.20.2</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>